{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.KindRatioFromBondLetters","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.KindRatioFromBondLetters","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KindRatioFromBondLetters.kind_ratios_eq_of_q_pow_four_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KindRatioFromBondLetters.kind_ratios_eq_of_q_pow_four_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KindRatioFromBondLetters.lean#L154-L168","doc":"**The derived weighting leaves the uniform locus.** If the two like-pair\nkind-ratios coincided, the carrier would be back on the uniform premise\n`BrunnianTripleExhaustion` assumes. They coincide only where `q⁴ = 1`, and the\nsubstrate `q₀ ≈ 1.10998` is not such a point — so the escape\n`KindDependentBondBreaksIntegrality` names is genuinely taken. Stated in the\ndirection that needs no characteristic hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KindRatioFromBondLetters.rho_pp_div_rho_nn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KindRatioFromBondLetters.rho_pp_div_rho_nn","kind":"theorem","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KindRatioFromBondLetters.lean#L142-L152","doc":"**The two like-pair kind-ratios differ by exactly `q⁴`.**\n\nThis is `BondLetterIdentification.nnFactor_eq_ppFactor_div_q_pow_four` seen\nthrough the `pn` reference: the `pn` letter cancels, so the relation holds\n**whatever** `t_pn` is — it does not depend on the production weight being\n`1/2 − δ/4`, only on `pp` and `nn` being `t = 0` and `t = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KindRatioFromBondLetters.rhoNN_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KindRatioFromBondLetters.rhoNN_eq","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KindRatioFromBondLetters.lean#L133-L140","doc":"**`ρ_nn = 12 q⁴ / P q`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KindRatioFromBondLetters.rhoPP_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KindRatioFromBondLetters.rhoPP_eq","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KindRatioFromBondLetters.lean#L124-L131","doc":"**`ρ_pp = 12 q⁸ / P q`.** The `pp` bond factor in units of the `pn` one —\nthe left-hand side `KindDependentBondBreaksIntegrality` asks for. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KindRatioFromBondLetters.bPN_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KindRatioFromBondLetters.bPN_eq","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KindRatioFromBondLetters.lean#L111-L122","doc":"**The derived `pn` letter IS the corpus's extracted constant.**\n\n`b_pn = P q / (12 q⁵ (q²+1))` — an identity of rational functions, not an\nagreement at `q₀`. The right-hand side is copied verbatim from\n`computations/qbeta/qbeta_bond_factors_derived_probe.py`, which obtained it by\nextraction from the 2H / 3H traces; the left-hand side is `tr_bond_interp` at the\nproduction weight. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KindRatioFromBondLetters.bondPoly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KindRatioFromBondLetters.bondPoly","kind":"def","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KindRatioFromBondLetters.lean#L106-L109","doc":"The degree-10 numerator that `qbeta_bond_factors_derived_probe` extracted. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KindRatioFromBondLetters.bNN","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KindRatioFromBondLetters.bNN","kind":"def","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KindRatioFromBondLetters.lean#L103-L104","doc":"`b_nn` — the `nn` bond factor, `tr_bond_ginv` at `t = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KindRatioFromBondLetters.bPN","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KindRatioFromBondLetters.bPN","kind":"def","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KindRatioFromBondLetters.lean#L100-L101","doc":"`b_pn` — the production `pn` bond factor, `tr_bond_interp` at `t = 1/2 − δ/4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KindRatioFromBondLetters.bPP","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KindRatioFromBondLetters.bPP","kind":"def","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KindRatioFromBondLetters.lean#L97-L98","doc":"`b_pp` — the `pp` bond factor, `BondLetterIdentification.tr_bond_gen` at `t = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KindRatioFromBondLetters.tPN","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KindRatioFromBondLetters.tPN","kind":"def","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KindRatioFromBondLetters.lean#L94-L95","doc":"The production `pn` mixing weight, ctype `averaged_weighted`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KindRatioFromBondLetters.flavorDelta","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KindRatioFromBondLetters.flavorDelta","kind":"def","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KindRatioFromBondLetters.lean#L91-L92","doc":"The substrate flavour split `δ = (q−1)²(1 − q⁻⁴)/3`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KindRatioFromBondLetters.hq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KindRatioFromBondLetters.hq","kind":"def","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KindRatioFromBondLetters.lean#L88-L89","doc":"The Hecke quadratic constant `h = q − q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KindRatioFromBondLetters.zD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KindRatioFromBondLetters.zD","kind":"def","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KindRatioFromBondLetters.lean#L85-L86","doc":"The convention-D Markov parameter `z = q³/(q²+1)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}